Hello Safety Team,

I am writing to report an adverse reaction in one of my patients, a 68-year-o=
ld male
(initials R.K.), who was taking Nortavex 40 mg once daily for the past 9 days.

Approximately 45 minutes after his ninth dose (taken 13-Aug-2026), the patien=
t developed
acute generalized urticaria and facial swelling. He was brought to our clinic=
 and then
transferred for observation; he was hospitalized for 18 hours and treated with
antihistamines and a corticosteroid. He has since been discharged and is reco=
vering well.

I have completed and attached our internal Adverse Event Report Form, which i=
ncludes his
lab values during the hospitalization (WBC, CRP, eosinophils) tracked over th=
ree days, as
well as full patient, reporter, and product details.

Please let me know if any additional information is needed.

Best regards,
Dr. Alina Foster
Meridian Family Health Clinic, Springvale
Treating Physician

